-- statement:
--   Certificate data for the horizontal argument change of $\zeta$ along the segment $\sigma\in[-1,2]$ at height $t=100000$.
--
--   The data are one record of the framework structure `Arb4.EdgeD`: the height, the Euler–Maclaurin cut $N=30000$, a log bound $L$, 41 octant pieces (`Arb4.PieceD`: a centre $\sigma_j=(a-b)/q$, a radius, an octant label, Taylor and remainder budgets) with breakpoints from $\sigma=2$ to $\sigma=-1$, two endpoint boxes and the final enclosure $[Lo,Hi]$ of $\arg\zeta$ change. The data were produced by a program and are not trusted; each piece is checked by the kernel in the problems `RHX100000.Edge.piece_00` … `piece_40`, the rest in `RHX100000.Edge.rest`.
-- source:
